Two changes from the previous attempt. The node no longer panics when the store has no usable entry, because that panic caused the `unreachable` trap. The parser now also accepts newline-, comma-, or JSON-array-style lists.

The store is only reachable through `get(key)`, and its key isn't specified, so I try `subscriptions`, `urls`, and `feeds` in turn. If none of them has a value, the node returns an empty list instead of failing. I can't tell whether `present(urls)` means "non-empty" or only "the field is set". If it means non-empty, an empty store would still violate it, and the node has no URLs to return in that case.

